{
  "schema": "camera.intro_shots/1",
  "_about": "The camera's shot families for the opening (docs/camera/varied-intros.md, docs/camera/varied-intros-data.md). A family is a short list of keyframes for one phase of the intro; the picker chooses one per phase and fighter from a hash of the match seed and the event's fields, never from the sim's random stream. Numbers are first values. Keyframe: t is the position in the shot (0 to 1 of the phase's span, which the event gives); cut true means a hard cut to this key (the shot opens on it), otherwise the camera eases from the key before; anchor is what the key is placed against (faller, lander, spot = the landing spot, crater, pair = the two fighters' middle, other = the other fighter, sky = straight up from the spot); dx and dy are body heights from the anchor (dy positive up); r is the subject's height as a share of the screen height; ay is where the anchor sits on the screen (0 top, 1 bottom); pitch is degrees (positive looks up; the ground rule limits a negative one to -6); fov is a multiplier of the field of view (1 is the game's). cuts counts the hard cuts the family makes; scroll is the worst share of the screen width the picture changes in a tick (measured or estimated); the picker refuses a family whose scroll is over the bound unless it is marked legacy.",
  "hash": {
    "algo": "fnv1a32",
    "fields": [
      "seed",
      "phase",
      "actor",
      "biome",
      "tod",
      "tone",
      "arrival",
      "template"
    ],
    "_note": "the fields are joined with a separator and hashed; u = hash / 2^32 picks by cumulative weight; the same context always gives the same family"
  },
  "constraints": {
    "maxCutsPerSecond": 3,
    "maxCutsInIntro": 8,
    "noRepeatPerPhase": 2,
    "scrollBound": 0.045,
    "faceMinStareTicks": 120
  },
  "defaults": {
    "fall": "F1",
    "descend": "D1",
    "land": "L1",
    "wait": "W1",
    "stare": "S1",
    "closing": "C1"
  },
